.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
data/cache/
data/*.parquet
data/raw/
data/*.csv
# Exception: append-only archive of pruned live_odds rows (see
# scripts/prune_live_data.py) -- committed deliberately. GitHub Actions runners
# have no persistent disk between runs, so an ignored file here would be
# silently lost after every workflow run. Text appends also compress far better
# in git history than the binary DB rewrites they relieve. No injuries_archive
# here -- unlike CFB, this build's `injuries` table is upserted (nflverse serves
# latest-status-per-player-week already), not append-only, so nothing to prune.
!data/live_odds_archive.csv
.DS_Store

# models/nfl_model.pkl (~5MB) is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike the CFB build's
# equivalent -- discovered live 2026-09-04 (Task 15's routine verification run)
# that a fresh clone with a gitignored model has NO model at all, forcing every
# scheduled routine run to retrain from scratch (scripts/train_model.py) before
# it can predict anything, adding several minutes per run for no benefit -- the
# model doesn't change between scheduled runs, only game_features grows. A
# committed, versioned pkl also means "the model in production" is a specific,
# reviewed artifact (visible in `git log -- models/`) rather than silently
# whatever train_model.py produces from current game_features on a given run.

# SQLite WAL sidecar files -- transient, never commit
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# Note: data/nfl_stats.db and data/nfl_predictions.db are deliberately NOT
# ignored. The two-DB split means only GitHub Actions ever writes nfl_stats.db
# and only the scheduled Claude routine writes nfl_predictions.db, so committing
# them as blobs avoids the Git LFS 403 the CFB build hit. Transient snapshot
# growth is handled by scripts/prune_live_data.py, not by ignoring the files.
